        {
          "id": "customer_churn_analysis.sql",
          "name": "customer_churn_analysis.sql",
          "kind": "sql_example",
          "provenance": "synthetic",
          "content": "-- Prepared sample; inspected as source code, not claimed to have been executed.\nWITH monthly_orders AS (\n  SELECT customer_id, DATE_TRUNC('month', order_date) AS month,\n         COUNT(*) AS orders, SUM(total) AS revenue\n  FROM orders GROUP BY customer_id, DATE_TRUNC('month', order_date)\n)\nSELECT customer_id, month, orders, revenue,\n       LAG(revenue) OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY month) AS previous_month_revenue\nFROM monthly_orders;"
        },
        {
          "id": "sales_analysis_project.md",
          "name": "sales_analysis_project.md",
          "kind": "calculation_table",
          "provenance": "synthetic",
          "content": "# Prepared sales calculation sample\n\nThis earlier application project is distinct from the targeted task dataset. Integer monthly totals support the calculations below; no business recommendation was supplied.\n\n| Month | Orders | Revenue AUD | Average order value AUD | Revenue change |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| April | 400 | 12000 | 30 | — |\n| May | 450 | 13500 | 30 | 12.50% |\n| June | 500 | 15000 | 30 | 11.11% |\n\nAverage order value = revenue / orders. Revenue change = (current revenue - previous revenue) / previous revenue. Percentages shown to two decimals. These calculations show descriptive comparison; they do not establish why revenue changed."
        },
        {
